  "rationale": "D3, data-informed revision on the fourth-generation droplet forward. The laws of D2 stand except in helium. A train-only error anatomy found 57 % of the train error in measurement artefacts, the hot-flame end timed well outside helium, and bands 2.5-4 times wider than the realised errors of clean cases. Changed: in helium the flame is lost sooner and what follows is written as a decaying cool flame (the published reading: 0.8 of the hot rate, transient at high dilution), which is what the three train helium runs show; the diffusive extinction is sharper; spreads are narrower; and a broad component is mixed in when the prefix shows an unstable tracker, above all a prefix D0 far from the sheet's. Every number typed by the author; no fit, no search; nothing chosen from validation.",
  "origin": "system"
}
